  "constraints": [
    "Preserve the W8A8 integer Gate/Up dot product, original per-channel and per-row scales, gate/up pairing, activation rounding, full 2304-channel row quantization and per-row scale before Down. Both matrix multiplications and their weights remain. Active LoRA, SITU, MXFP and distributed wrappers have separate contracts.",
    "One or both intermediates would be kept on chip across the original operators. The full row reduction, cross-core exchange, buffering and Cube/vector utilization may remove the savings. Reported values price the removable traffic; they do not bound launch savings or prove admission on hardware.",
    "C8 moves the latest 16-rank ForeachAddList input-consumer start per layer under the archived clock bounds with all subsequent work translating. Measured task durations cap each original stage once. Both-half-credit is a sensitivity. The first four scenarios credit only the two buffer boundaries. The optimistic absorb_activation_and_gaps scenario additionally prices zero incremental activation arithmetic, its full original task and both intervening spans (even if they contain required work), without double counting its buffer traffic. It freezes both GEMMs except for the saved store/load. No F21 time, expert assignment or weight traffic is credited.",
    "C8 includes the request’s own first prompt wave and eligible graph ordinals, using 40 times the median graph-site estimate per ordinal. The four-wave ordering, histogram and clock assumptions are historical; an external reader or independent branch may mask all gains.",
    "Ordinary user requests use their recorded eager per-rank extent as the shared expert extent and count their verification batches at M3. Eager time uses a linear uncapped traffic proxy with no direct matching shape timing. All credited time reaches that request. No production traffic weighting."
